# RoadWatch API Reference

Base URL: `http://localhost:8000`
Interactive docs (Swagger UI): `http://localhost:8000/docs`

---

## Endpoints

### GET /health
Returns `{"status": "ok"}`. Use to confirm the server is running.

---

### GET /api/complaints
Returns all complaints, newest first.

**Query params:**
| Param | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `status_filter` | string (optional) | Filter by status e.g. `Reported`, `Verified` |

**Response:** array of Complaint objects (see schema below).

---

### POST /api/complaints
Submit a new pothole report. Runs YOLO detection automatically.

**Body:** `multipart/form-data`
| Field | Type | Required |
|-------|------|----------|
| `photo` | file | ✅ |
| `latitude` | float | ✅ |
| `longitude` | float | ✅ |
| `description` | string | ❌ |
| `device_token` | string | ❌ (FCM token for push notifications) |

**Response:** Complaint object with `severity`, `ai_confidence`, `ai_summary` filled in.

---

### GET /api/complaints/{id}
Returns one complaint by UUID.

---

### PATCH /api/complaints/{id}
Update status, department, or notes. Used by Admin Dashboard.

**Body:** `application/json`
```json
{
  "status": "Verified",
  "assigned_department": "Public Works Department",
  "notes": "Field team dispatched"
}
```
All fields optional — only send what you want to change.
Triggers FCM push notification to reporter if `status` changes.

---

### DELETE /api/complaints/{id}
Deletes a complaint (spam / duplicate removal).

---

## Complaint schema

```json
{
  "id": "uuid",
  "image_url": "/uploads/abc123.jpg",
  "latitude": 28.6139,
  "longitude": 77.2090,
  "description": "Large pothole near junction",

  "severity": "High",
  "ai_confidence": 0.87,
  "detections_count": 3,
  "ai_summary": "Detected 3 pothole region(s). Largest covers 42.1% of frame.",

  "status": "Verified",
  "assigned_department": "Public Works Department",
  "notes": null,

  "created_at": "2026-08-24T10:30:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-24T11:00:00"
}
```

## Status flow
```
Reported → Verified → Assigned → Repair in Progress → Resolved
```

## Severity levels
| Level | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| Low | Small crack or minor pothole — monitor |
| Medium | Moderate pothole — schedule repair |
| High | Large / dangerous pothole — urgent repair |
